PRIORITY='''PRIORITY LAYOUT CORRECTION — overrides existing cover layout and all contradictory details: do not create an enlarged poster. This is a calm110px collectible card next to the approved references. Compact Kodak wordmark with the letters only about6–7percent of canvas height, usually at x=6percent,y=7percent in a header18percent high, or compact bottom brand strip if actual packaging dictates. Never use the oversized Kodak from old Image1. Main stock title block is inset at least8percent from both edges, maximum84percent total width, centered within y=34–65percent; each title line11–14percent canvas height at most. Use2–3 lines for long stock names. Secondary descriptions like Color Negative Film or Professional are small supporting text, never extra big headlines. The footer is ALL one consistent small size:24–28px on1024px square, with8percent bottom/right margin. ABSOLUTELY NO large120,220,620,828 or35mm: these are technical format values, not film speeds. Treat footer exactly as a tiny caption, format no larger than ISO/process. No invented white paragraphs. Smooth uniform paper texture with minimal grain, no strong blotches. Use flat ink throughout. Preserve each edition's genuine brand mark; historical EASTMAN labels stay EASTMAN, not a modern KODAK substitute.

'''
COMMON='''Use case: style-transfer. Asset: ONE standalone square full-bleed flat printed film-cover illustration, for the JustShoot Library grid.
INPUT ROLES: Image1 = existing app cover to EDIT; retain its exact stock/edition identity but correct its invented decorations and inaccurate lettering using Image2. Image2 = exact REAL PACKAGING SCAN for this edition, authoritative for era, stock name, real typography, color blocks and motif; extract front-panel identity, never reproduce the unfolded carton. Image3 = APPROVED Portra400 app cover, authority for refined flat print, fine paper grain, clean spacing and readable type hierarchy only; DO NOT transplant its purple palette, layout, brand position or stock title into unrelated films. Image4 = approved Fuji cover, secondary authority for matching the app's visual texture and calm spacing ONLY; do NOT include FUJIFILM brand, green header or Velvia title.
Redesign Image1 to sit harmoniously alongside the approved cards: authentic edition-specific palette and type, generous 6percent safe margins, concise product name in middle region, compact era-correct Kodak brand, very small technical footer (2.4–3percent of square height). Main title should remain legible at110px; long names can use2–3 carefully spaced lines. Stock speed is prominent only as part of actual product name; format numbers120/220/620/828 or bulk length must NEVER become headline. Brand around10percent canvas height at most. Keep authentic curved bands/straight geometry; remove unsupported ribbons, fans, arrows, colored chips, filmstrips and empty promotional badges. Let genuine secondary-color title panels occupy a meaningful35–60percent when appropriate, instead of placing tiny colored logo on yet another orange square. For genuinely historical all-yellow labels retain yellow and era typography; do not invent color diversity. Use one harmonious warm Kodak yellow family (not glowing orange), navy/cobalt, burgundy, muted plum or forest green only where this edition supports them.
Texture: delicate uniform paper fibers, very low contrast. Entirely FLAT INK, absolutely no 3D extrusions, beveled/embossed letters, foil, metallic shine, glossy shapes, folded fabric, casts shadows, external shadow, lighting gradients or heavy vignette. Muted gold means flat mustard printing ink. Square full bleed, outer corners square because the app clips them.
No JustShoot, RAW, sRGB, workflow arrows, FilmSimulation text, invented slogans, new product names, expiry dates, barcodes, noisy microtext paragraphs, photographs or 3Dboxes. Do not draw four covers, a grid, a collage, a mockup screen, or reference labels. Only the requested single cover. All spelling and stock suffixes must be exact. Omit unknown values rather than printing UNKNOWN or N/A.
'''
jobs=[]
for c in ROWS:
 cid=c['id'];key=cid[:5]
 if cid in ['00200_000','00244_000']:
  jobs.append({'id':cid,'kind':'reuse-approved','source':'cover_kodak_portra_400.heic','reason':'Matching 35mm36EXP curved purple-band PORTRA400 edition already approved.','status':'pending'})
  continue
 footer=c['format']
 if c['quantity'] not in ['Unknown','N/A',None]:footer+=' · '+c['quantity']
 if c['iso'] is not None:footer+=' · ISO '+str(c['iso'])
 if c['process'] not in ['Unknown','N/A',None]:footer+=' · '+c['process']
 prompt=PRIORITY+COMMON+f"\nEXACT PRODUCT: {c['product']}. Stock ISO: {c['iso'] if c['iso'] is not None else 'not specified; do not invent'}. Small technical footer (only): {footer}. Catalog edition/format: {c['subtype']}.\nINDIVIDUAL ART DIRECTION: {D[key]}\nCorrect any typos present in the existing generated cover by consulting this exact product name and packaging scan. Output a crisp square 1024by1024 cover."
 refs=[str(ART/'before'/(cid+'.png')),str(ART/'references'/(cid+'.jpg')),str(ART/'styles/cover_kodak_portra_400.png'),str(ART/'styles/cover_fuji_velvia.png')]
 jobs.append({'id':cid,'kind':'generate','status':'pending','prompt':prompt,'references':refs,'direction':D[key]})
(REPORT/'jobs.json').write_text(json.dumps(jobs,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
print(json.dumps({'jobs':len(jobs),'generate':sum(j['kind']=='generate' for j in jobs),'reuse':sum(j['kind']=='reuse-approved' for j in jobs)}))
